/* ── The dashboard parts: action tiles, status rows, the facet list, the heat grid, the matrix, the bar in a cell, the
   week agenda and the run timeline [kpadopt2] ──
   Titanium's own (themes/titanium/CHARACTER.md): a tile is a machined plate, square with the register's chamfer pair
   (top-start and bottom-end), the bright tool edge along its top (G7, G8); every contact is instant and linear, metal
   does not ease (G1, G4): pointing turns the tool edge to bare bright metal, a press drops the plate 1 px; a pick is
   bright metal, a running process blue oxide (G6); waiting is the anodising bath, the oxide ramp drifting start to end
   in every waiting part (G10); Martian Mono for labels and counts (G8). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The dashboard parts: what the package leaves to a register [kpadopt2-repairs] ──
   Formal keeps these parts exactly as Kenny approved them; this theme takes the three repairs the review asks for: a
   loading heat grid or matrix row as tall as its ready row (no skeleton gap between cells), an empty or failed run
   timeline with a lane-sized space for its sentence (never over the legend), the sentence as wide as its words on the
   theme's ground (never through a rule or a ghost bar), and an axis label near the end edge standing before its rule. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The six opt-in options of the dashboard adoption, round 3, in this theme [kpadopt3] ──
   The nav bar's separator, the timeline's day buttons and series runs, the week agenda's upcoming list on a phone and
   the facet swatch's identity pattern (the choice-filter value and the heat grid's End are behaviour only).
   Titanium's own (themes/titanium/CHARACTER.md): the separator is the divider's milled groove stood
   upright, a dark channel with its bright lip; lying down across the phone's list it is the groove itself. A day on the
   axis has its tool edge turned to bright metal under the pointer, instantly (G1); pressed it is a blue-oxide plate with
   the chamfer pair, the oxide edge under it. A series' finished run carries its tool edge along the top in its own
   oxide; the facet pattern is chamfered. Every contact is linear. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in titanium's grammar: data pieces, empty-state drawings [kpadopt4] ──
   Titanium's own (themes/titanium/CHARACTER.md): a part is machined, never moulded: square with the chamfer pair (top
   start and bottom end, cut outwards past the box so a ring or a shadow stays whole, G7), a bright tool edge along its
   top, engraved Martian Mono for labels and figures (G8); contact is instant and linear, pointing turns the tool edge to
   bare bright metal, a press drops the part 1 px (G1, G4, G6); the oxide is a cause only: blue is what the system says,
   gold to cyan is heat, and a loading part is in the anodising bath (G5, G9, G10). Every drawing in an empty state is a
   part on a machinist's drawing, cut in from the start edge and cooling from the oxide's heat colours to bare metal. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in titanium's grammar: rows, tiles, check lists, pipeline, journey, secret, dialog [kpadopt4] ──
   A row's state is a bar cut along its start edge: bare metal for what is new to the person, blue oxide for what the
   system is doing, gold for a reservation, bronze for a failure (G5, G6); the lists between rows are milled grooves. A
   tile of choices is a machined plate whose ticked edge is bare metal; a lane of the pipeline is a plate with an oxide
   strip along its head; a journey is a rail whose reached stretch is oxide cut in start to end; a secret is fed into its
   pocket from the start edge and its countdown is the film cooling away (G2, G11); a dialog's danger section is the
   bronze tool edge along its top (the register's destructive). Every contact is instant and linear, a press drops 1 px. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in titanium's grammar: time, cooking and comparison [kpadopt4] ──
   A time read out is engraved in a pocket in Martian Mono, instant and linear (G1, G8); a running process is blue oxide,
   what the system says (G6); a finished timer is the bronze tool edge along its top and never breathes (G5); the timer
   disc is a turned part, its face with turning grain and the time left a sector of bare metal; the wheel is an indexing
   head that settles on the theme's one curve (G1); a three-way chip is a machined key whose state is a square mark; the
   quantity's figure and the checklist's amounts are Martian Mono; the compare slider is a parting line with a turned
   knob. Contact is 60 ms linear, a press drops the part 1 px. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── kpadopt4 repairs found at 390 px [kpadopt4] ──
   A label set in this theme's wide letters needs more room than the aside leaves it in a narrow form: below 36rem of the
   form's own width each row is its own column (label, control, then the aside under it), so no label ever runs into the aside. The countdown's
   colon takes the room of a monospaced character. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── A sort the page carries out [kpadopt4]: the sorted header is edged in bare metal (G6) ──
